  ---                                                                                                                                 
   
  ## Preconditions                                                                                                                    
                                          
  The user must provide a list of URLs to analyze. If they haven't, ask for them before starting.
                                                                                                                                      
  Identify one page as the **parent** (top of the silo — usually the broadest or highest in the site hierarchy). The rest are
  **supporting pages**. If the user hasn't specified which is the parent, infer it from the URL structure (shortest path = parent) and
   confirm before proceeding.
                                                                                                                                      
  ---             
                                                                                                                                      
  ## Step 1 — Extract Content from Each Page

  Use Playwright to navigate to each URL and extract the main body content.
                                          
  **1a. Find the content container.**         
                                                                                                                                      
  ```javascript
  () => {                                                                                                                             
    const selectors = [
      '#pageContentContainer', '.entry-content', '.post-content',                                                                     
      'article', 'main', '#main-content', '.content', '#content'
    ];                                        
    return selectors.map(sel => {         
      const el = document.querySelector(sel);                                                                                         
      return { sel, found: !!el, textLength: el ? el.innerText.trim().length : 0 };                                                   
    });                                                                                                                               
  }                                                                                                                                   
  ```             
                                                                                                                                      
  Pick the selector with the most text that is clearly the main content (not nav/footer/sidebar).
                                                                                                                                      
  **1b. Extract text and metadata.**          
                                                                                                                                      
  ```javascript
  () => {                                                                                                                             
    const container = document.querySelector('#pageContentContainer') || document.querySelector('main') || document.body;
    const headings = Array.from(document.querySelectorAll('h1, h2, h3')).map(h => ({                                                  
      level: h.tagName, text: h.innerText.trim()
    }));                                  
    return {                                                                                                                          
      url: window.location.href,                                                                                                      
      title: document.title,                                                                                                          
      headings,                                                                                                                       
      text: container.innerText.trim().replace(/\s+/g, ' ')
    };                                                                                                                                
  }                                       
  ```                                                                                                                                 
                                                                                                                                      
  **1c. Extract and test hyperlinks from body copy.**
                                                                                                                                      
  After extracting text, fetch the raw HTML and extract all `<a href>` elements from the main content container (excluding nav,
  header, footer, sidebar). For each link record the anchor text, href, and whether it is internal (munley.com) or external. Skip     
  `mailto:`, `tel:`, and anchor (`#`) links — these are not testable URLs.
                                                                                                                                      
  ```python       
  from bs4 import BeautifulSoup                                                                                                       
  import urllib.request                       
                                          
  # Load saved HTML, strip nav/header/footer/sidebar/script/style
  # container = #pageContentContainer or main or body                                                                                 
  # links = [(a.get_text(strip=True), a['href']) for a in container.find_all('a', href=True)
  #           if a.get_text(strip=True) and not a['href'].startswith(('mailto:', 'tel:', '#'))]                                       
  ```                                         
                                                                                                                                      
  **Test every link with a HEAD request** (fall back to GET if HEAD is refused). Use a 10-second timeout. Record the HTTP status code 
  for each URL. Classify as:                                                                                                          
                                                                                                                                      
  - **Broken** — 4xx or 5xx response (flag in report)                                                                                 
  - **Redirect** — 3xx response; note the final destination if it differs significantly from the original href (e.g., redirects to
  homepage = likely broken)                                                                                                           
  - **OK** — 200 response                                                                                                             
   
  ```python                                                                                                                           
  import urllib.request, urllib.error     
                                                                                                                                      
  def check_link(url, timeout=10):                                                                                                    
      req = urllib.request.Request(url, method='HEAD',
            headers={'User-Agent': 'Mozilla/5.0'})                                                                                    
      try:                                
          resp = urllib.request.urlopen(req, timeout=timeout)
          return resp.status, resp.url                                                                                                
      except urllib.error.HTTPError as e: 
          if e.code == 405:  # HEAD not allowed, try GET                                                                              
              req2 = urllib.request.Request(url,                                                                                      
                     headers={'User-Agent': 'Mozilla/5.0'})
              try:                                                                                                                    
                  resp2 = urllib.request.urlopen(req2, timeout=timeout)                                                               
                  return resp2.status, resp2.url
              except urllib.error.HTTPError as e2:                                                                                    
                  return e2.code, url         
          return e.code, url                                                                                                          
      except Exception as ex:
          return str(ex), url                                                                                                         
  ```
                                                                                                                                      
  After testing, flag the following during analysis:
  - **Broken links** — any link returning 4xx or 5xx, or a 3xx that resolves to the site homepage
  - **Attorney bio blocks with no link** — bio block names an attorney but does not hyperlink to their `/our-attorneys/[name]/` page
  - **Weak anchor text on internal links** — anchor text is generic ("click here", "learn more", "here", or a bare URL)               
  - **Mismatched internal links** — internal link goes to a different practice area than the page topic when a more relevant page
  exists                                                                                                                              
  - **Contradictory external sources** — two external links on the same page cite different figures for the same claim without        
  explaining the discrepancy                                                                                                          
                                                                                                                                      
  Report link findings under a **Links** section in the per-page report. List broken links first, then content issues. Omit the       
  section entirely if no issues are found.                                                                                            
                  
  Repeat steps 1a–1c for every URL. Store all results before moving to analysis.                                                      
                                          
